WEBVTT

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.540
<b>The Island of the 
Everlasting Cherry Blossom</b>

00:01:59.000 --> 00:01:59.990
Ricca-san.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:00.970
What?

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.250
What's going on?

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:04.060
Why did you suddenly 
call us all together?

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:05.720
Did something happen?

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.690
Just follow me.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:19.490
Sakura?

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:21.910
Ah, Sakura-chan!

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:24.080
Hello everyone, it's been a while.

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.510
We haven't all been together since 
we went to the pool, have we?

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:28.410
We haven't.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.210
Sakura.

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:35.980
I was worried about you.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:39.680
Onii-chan...

00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:48.430
Ricca-san, did you call us all out here
 so we could see Sakura-chan?

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:51.620
Yeah. Sakura said she 
wanted to see everyone.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:53.170
All of us?

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:55.490
Sakura, did something happen?

00:02:56.090 --> 00:02:58.440
Yes. Actually,

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:03.120
I'm going away today.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.540
Going away?

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:13.630
I've made up my mind.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:15.990
Sakura...

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:21.260
So, could we all play together today?

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:22.510
Ah, but...

00:03:22.510 --> 00:03:23.680
Well, why not?

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.510
Ricca-san?

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:29.220
Let's all help make one last,
 fun memory for her!

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:33.180
She's right. I don't like sad farewells.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.180
Let's all have fun together!

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:36.340
That sounds good.

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:36.940
Yes.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:42.400
But where should we go to have fun?

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.260
Should we go to the pool?

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:45.480
Again?

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:49.240
Sakura-chan, is there 
anywhere you want to go?

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.080
Sakura Shopping District

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.520
Sheep
2000 yen

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.520
Black Cat
2000 yen

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:52.770
We'll do this here... And that'll do it!

00:04:56.950 --> 00:04:58.010
Tada!

00:04:59.130 --> 00:04:59.980
Huh?

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.950
Isn't this kind of awful?

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.190
My eyes aren't that big.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:05.570
Now, now.

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:07.060
Please retake it!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.160
Onii-chan, let's take one together.

00:05:13.330 --> 00:05:16.330
Aw, Sakura-chan, no fair!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:17.900
Sheesh, Charles-san...

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:21.840
I want a picture of me and Taka-kun, too!

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.390
Just let her do it today.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.760
Onii-chan, this way, this way!

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:35.790
Onii-chan.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:38.440
Smile.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:41.050
Right...

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.280
Cheers!

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:50.620
This is all we can do, but...

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:52.640
I'm having lots of fun!

00:05:52.640 --> 00:05:53.950
So am I!

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:55.750
Sorry for the wait.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.660
Wow, incredible!

00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:01.220
What is this?

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:02.360
Japanese sweets?

00:06:02.360 --> 00:06:04.080
Was this even on the menu?

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.560
Th-This is a...

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:08.900
Sakura-chan, I heard you 
like Japanese sweets,

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.050
so I had it made especially for you.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:13.020
Let's hurry up and eat it!

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.750
It's delicious!

00:06:23.890 --> 00:06:25.470
Here, your share, Utamaru.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.910
Yeah, it's great!

00:06:32.060 --> 00:06:36.140
I don't usually eat Japanese sweets,
 but this is pretty good.

00:06:36.140 --> 00:06:38.150
I might get hooked on this.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:45.600
But if you like Japanese sweets, 
you must have pretty grown-up tastes.

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:47.350
You think so?

00:06:49.830 --> 00:06:51.760
It'll be lonely...

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.640
Without you here anymore...

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:02.670
And just when I thought 
we'd become friends, too...

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.290
Friends...

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:08.250
I'm your friend, too!

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:11.320
We're all your friends from 
now on, too, Sakura-chan.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.020
Thank you.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:25.980
Ricca-san.

00:07:25.980 --> 00:07:26.830
What?

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:28.660
What happened?

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:31.560
Why did Sakura suddenly 
decide to leave this island?

00:07:33.660 --> 00:07:35.970
Ricca-san, do you know why?

00:07:37.690 --> 00:07:41.100
I only learned yesterday 
that she'd be leaving us.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.400
This is what Sakura's decided,

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.520
so I want to watch over her.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.560
It's beautiful.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:01.870
It really is.

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:05.170
But we should've brought our swimsuits 
if we were going to the beach.

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:08.360
It's still too early to go in the water.

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:10.550
That's right. You'll catch a cold.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.210
Oh, you're right.

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:13.770
Utamaru, let's go!

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.850
Sakura?

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:19.800
Eek, it's cold!

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.150
Let's go, too!

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:25.170
Ricca?

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:28.230
You're right.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:29.630
Shall we?

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:31.260
We did come to the beach.

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:33.610
Let's have fun, too!

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:37.720
Your voice and that smile

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:41.360
are as precious as the first time.

00:08:42.140 --> 00:08:46.690
My feelings race towards

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:49.420
the distance in the endless sky.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:53.600
When the cherry blossoms 
dance in the wind,

00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:57.330
the feelings that come and go

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:02.640
with their glitter and fragrance

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:05.070
guide me here.

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:09.420
I wish that I could say

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:13.560
"I love you!"

00:09:14.710 --> 00:09:18.370
If I tuck away my wishes

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:21.450
and the pieces of our conversations,

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:25.330
my heart suddenly aches

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:29.460
and I hide it all away.

00:09:30.730 --> 00:09:35.490
The light raining down,

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.970
where is it heading?

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:48.270
You can see all of 
Hatsune Island from here.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.570
From here it seems like a small island.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.320
I wonder where my house is.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:01.410
Your apartment complex is over there, so...

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:04.420
There are so many houses, 
it's hard to find.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:07.060
That area over there used to be a plaza.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:09.170
Oh, now I remember.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:11.660
Remember what, Nii-san?

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.550
When you fell down in that plaza.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:18.340
I had a hard time getting you to stop crying.

00:10:18.570 --> 00:10:20.700
Something like that happened?

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.380
Jeez, Nii-san...

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:26.190
That's not fair, enjoying memories 
just between the two of you!

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:31.230
There are a lot of memories in many 
places because it's such a small island.

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.410
Well, it's time for us to be going.

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.450
Later, Sakura-chan.

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:50.930
Take care.

00:10:52.320 --> 00:10:53.080
Yes...

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:06.970
I'll lend him to you for a bit longer.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:14.040
Come on, everyone, let's go.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:15.270
Ricca?

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:16.900
Please wait, Ricca-san.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:32.760
Onii-chan.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:34.980
What is it?

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:41.460
It's almost time to say goodbye 
to you, too, Onii-chan...

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.140
Sakura...

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:48.640
Before the end...

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:02.700
Let's go on a date!

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:04.910
Huh? A date?

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:17.410
A date! A date! A date with Nii-chan!

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:19.050
Hey, Sakura...

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:20.730
There's nothing to be embarrassed about.

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:21.720
We're on a date.

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:22.850
But...

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:25.780
Hmm, where should we go?

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:34.720
Hm? What is it?

00:12:35.260 --> 00:12:36.900
Onii-chan, come here...

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:45.910
Sheesh.

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:47.400
How is this...

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:49.930
a date?

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:51.200
Don't worry about it.

00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.190
I love the view of the ocean from here.

00:13:03.690 --> 00:13:07.480
Speaking of which, this is where 
we first met each other, isn't it?

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:10.380
You were staring at the ocean,

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:12.460
and looked confused when 
I called out to you...

00:13:13.070 --> 00:13:14.750
I still remember it well.

00:13:15.960 --> 00:13:16.980
Me, too...

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:24.150
Hey, Sakura.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.150
What happened?

00:13:29.650 --> 00:13:32.060
Why are you suddenly bidding farewell...

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:33.410
Ow, ow!

00:13:34.430 --> 00:13:36.200
What are you doing, Sakura?!

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:38.500
Onii-chan, smile.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.000
We're on a date.

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.920
It's no fun if you look like that.

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:45.980
You're right.

00:13:46.340 --> 00:13:47.260
Besides,

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:53.350
I want to bid farewell to you 
with a smile, Onii-chan.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:54.830
Sakura...

00:13:56.650 --> 00:13:57.350
Okay?

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:00.450
Okay.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:05.250
Then, where should we go next?

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.210
Kazami Academy

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:11.000
It's closed today.

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:15.720
If I remember, over here...

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:25.800
I never knew there was a hole over 
there you could get in through.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:29.340
I know a lot of details about this school.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.370
Hey, let's go over there.

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:46.610
H-Huh?

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:49.780
Congratulations on Graduation

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:50.650
Yeah, our graduation party
 is coming up soon.

00:14:51.270 --> 00:14:52.990
They've already started preparing for it.

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:56.160
That's kind of sad.

00:14:56.930 --> 00:14:57.760
Is it?

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:02.880
Well, graduation is also 
the day we set off, so...

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:07.010
Onii-chan, what are you 
going to be in the future?

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.320
Huh? Me?

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:11.740
I haven't decided yet...

00:15:11.740 --> 00:15:13.180
What about you, Sakura?

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:15.560
Huh? I...

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:18.580
Sakura?

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:21.570
It's a secret.

00:15:28.480 --> 00:15:29.960
It's beautiful, isn't it?

00:15:31.220 --> 00:15:32.680
I'm so happy.

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.620
I've made lots of friends.

00:15:36.510 --> 00:15:39.580
And in the end, I got to on 
a date with you, Onii-chan.

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:41.250
Sakura...

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:43.810
You're right.

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:48.980
I guess I should tell you, Onii-chan.

00:16:20.310 --> 00:16:21.260
This is...

00:16:23.160 --> 00:16:24.830
The Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:28.820
A magic tree that will grant any wish.

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:44.810
Hey, Onii-chan,

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:47.550
can you make me a promise?

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:08.080
And on that day,

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:12.610
when the cherry blossoms bloomed 
for the first time in 20 years,

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:17.600
I appeared here once again...

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.860
This isn't the place I belong.

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:32.630
I'm about to go meet someone 
who was very important to me.

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:34.860
Someone important to you?

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:38.350
I don't know if I'll be able to see him, but...

00:17:41.940 --> 00:17:42.700
You will.

00:17:44.640 --> 00:17:47.620
I'm sure your feelings will reach him.

00:17:53.030 --> 00:17:55.110
You really do resemble him...

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.300
The man who's important to me...

00:17:58.800 --> 00:17:59.990
What kind of person is he?

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:03.720
Someone who often said, "It's a pain,"

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:05.940
but,

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:08.940
who was also very kind...

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:11.230
I see...

00:18:17.080 --> 00:18:18.200
I'm going now.

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.700
Come back whenever you want.

00:18:30.350 --> 00:18:33.910
I'll always be your friend, Sakura.

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:36.220
Onii-chan...

00:18:39.060 --> 00:18:43.350
I'm glad I met you, Onii-chan.

00:18:45.370 --> 00:18:46.300
Sakura...

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:37.110
Thank you.

00:20:29.680 --> 00:20:31.330
What a pain...

00:20:36.710 --> 00:20:39.090
Onii-chan!

00:23:06.980 --> 00:23:10.370
<i>Tomorrow evening, come to the 
Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree.</i>

00:23:25.050 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Da Capo</b>

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:28.580
One promise and a modest wish.

00:23:28.970 --> 00:23:31.680
Unchanging for decades, even centuries.

00:23:31.960 --> 00:23:33.130
A precious feeling.

00:23:33.950 --> 00:23:35.760
Final Episode: Da Capo

00:23:36.350 --> 00:23:39.300
A miracle that's crossed time 
is about to repeat once more.
